-- Fixture for the `l4 export --fail-on=SEVERITY` threshold tests.
--
-- `--fail-on` means "exit non-zero when the report holds a note THIS SEVERE OR
-- WORSE", and FidelitySeverity is ordered Blocking < Lossy < Advisory, so the
-- gate compares `<=`. Testing that on a report whose notes are all Blocking
-- only pins one end: every threshold trips, so an implementation that trips on
-- any note at all, or one whose comparison runs the other way, still passes.
--
-- This module is the other end. Its DMN export carries exactly one note, and
-- that note is ADVISORY (D-ORDERDEPENDENT: hit policy First over more than one
-- row is order-dependent). So `--fail-on=advisory` must exit non-zero while
-- `--fail-on=lossy` and `--fail-on=blocking` must exit 0 — with notes present
-- the whole time, which is what makes "no note is severe enough" observable
-- rather than indistinguishable from "no notes".
--
-- Kept to a guarded chain deliberately: a formula-shaped decision would draw a
-- Blocking D-LITERALEXPR and destroy the property this fixture exists for.

DECLARE Band IS ONE OF Low, Mid, High

GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`band` MEANS
       IF   income AT MOST 1000
       THEN Low
       ELSE IF   income AT MOST 5000
            THEN Mid
            ELSE High
